<--------------> Props Drilling <------------------>
Props drilling ek aisi situation hai jahan data ko kisi deep child component tak pohanchane ke liye usay darmiyan wale tamam levels (intermediate components)
 se zabardasti pass karna parta hai, chahe unhe us data ki zaroorat na bhi ho.

 App
 |
 |
 parent
 |
 |
 child
|
|
grandparent

the user object is passed through every components

1: - App.jsx file:
import Parent from "./Components/Parent"

function App(){
  const studentName='ali'
  return(
    <>
  
    <h1>react prop drilling</h1>
    <Parent studentName={studentName} />

    </>
  )
}
export default App


2: - parent.jsx file:
import Child from "./Child"
function Parent({studentName}){
    return(
        <>
        <div style={{border:"2px solid blue",padding:'10px',margin:'10px'}}>
        <h2>this is parents  Components</h2>
        {/* passing the prop to child */}
        <Child studentName={studentName}/>
        </div>
        </>
    )
}
export default Parent

3: - child.jsx file:
// prop drilling
import GrandChild from "./GrandChild"
function Child({studentName}){
    return(
        <>
        <div style={{border:'2px solid blue', margin:'10px', padding:'10px'}}>
            <h2>child Components</h2>
            {/* passing the same prop agian */}
            <GrandChild studentName={studentName} />
        </div>
        </>
    )
}
export  default Child

4: - GrandChild.jsx file:
function GrandChild({studentName}){
    return(
        <>
        <div style={{border:'2px solid red',margin:'10px', padding:'10px'}}>
            <h2>Grandchild Components</h2>
            <h3>student Name :{studentName}</h3>
        </div>
        </>
    )
}
export default GrandChild

<-------------------------------> UseState (hook) <--------------------------------->
useStae:
useState ek React Hook hai jo functional components me dynamic data (state)
 ko track aur update karne ki ijazat deta hai taake data badalne par screen automatically 
 re-render ho jaye.

 // 1: - useState.jsx file:
 import { useState } from "react";
function UseState(){
  const[count,setCount]=useState(0)
  return(
    <>
    <h1>{count}</h1>
    <button onClick={()=>setCount(count+1)}>press this</button>
    </>
  )
}
export default UseState


/// 2: - App.jsx(file):
import UseState from "./Components/UseState"

function App(){
  return(
    <>
    <UseState />
    </>
  )
}
export default App


<-----------------> state with object <-------------------->
/// 1 : - object need :

React mein objects (ya state) ki zaroorat isliye parti hai taake hum aik se 
zyada related data/values ko aik sath organize aur manage kar sakein.

/// 2 : - spread operator :
Spread operator (...) aik JavaScript feature hai jo kisi array ya object ke saare elements ko khol kar 
(unpack karke) naye array ya object mein copy karne ke liye use hota hai.

/// Note for spread operator :-
Spread operator (...) purane data ki ek new copy banata hai, 
us mein naye items ya changes add karta hai, aur ek hi line mein original
 data ko disturb kiye baghair naye data se update kar deta hai.

<-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------->

<---------------------------> State Lifting <---------------------------------------->
/// State Lifting : -
State lifting React mein child components se data ko unke common 
parent component mein move karne ko kehte hain taake wo 
data dono ya sabhi sibling components mein share ho sake.


// why need state lifting : -
State lifting ki zaroorat isliye pari kyun ke React mein data sirf
 upar se neeche (parent to child) flow hota hai, isliye sibling components ko
 aapas mein data share karne ke liye ek common parent ki zaroorat hoti hai.


<--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------->
<-------------------------------> event Handling in react <------------------------------------>
// difference between html and react event:
// 1: Html event:-
HTML events browser ke native event handling ko lowercase mein use karte hain (jaise onclick), 
<button onclick='sayhello()'>click me </button>

// 2 : - React event : -
jabki 
React events synthetic events ka use karte hain jo cross-browser compatibility ke 
liye camelCase mein likhe jaate hain (jaise onClick).
<button onClick={hello}>click me </button>

//3 : synthetic event :-
Synthetic events React ka apna ek wrapper hain jo browser ke native events ko lapet kar sabhi browsers 
(Chrome, Safari, Firefox) mein ek jaisa aur smooth kaam karne ki sahulat deta hai.

 <button onClick={greet()}>say hello</button> <-- functional call automatically output when page reload

  <button onClick={greet}>say hello</button> <-- reference call output see when click button 


  <---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------->
  <--------------------> Forms <------------------------------------->
  // Forms:
  Form ek aisa interactive element hai jiske zariye user se input data (jaise text, email, password)
   collect karke server ya component state mein submit kiya jata hai.

<------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------->
<--------------------------------> Handle UI <------------------------------------------------->
// 1: Handle UI :-
UI handling ka matlab hai user ke actions (jaise click, type, ya scroll) ke mutabiq screen par
 dikhne wale interface (UI) ko dynamic tareeqe se update aur manage karna.

useeffect use for api call perform krni ho

<---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------->
<------------------------------> Use Effect <--------------------------------------------------->

// 1  : - useeffect:
useEffect React ka ek built-in hook hai jo component ke render hone ke baad external operations 
(side effects) jaise data fetching, API calls, timers set karne,
 ya DOM ko manually update karne ke liye use hota ha

// Basic Structure:
useEffect(()=>{
  // side Effect
},[])

useEffect require two parameter one is arrow function, dependency array.

// useEffect clean up function: (is arrow function my kuch return kr rhy hoty hain):
useEffect(()=>{
  // side Effect
  console.log('mounted')
  return() =>{
    // clean up function
    console.log('unmpunted')
  }
},[])

[]= dependency array my hum wo value dety hain k jb bi value change hoto useEffect re-render ho 
    agr na dy to hum sirf ek dafa useEffect chaly ga. or agr dependency array na dy to hum infinite 
    loop my phas jae gy


// clean up function:
useEffect ka clean-up function ek aesa return function hota hai jo
 component ke unmount (remove) hone par ya agle render ke chalne 
 se pehle purane effects (jaise active timers, event listeners,
 ya subscription subscriptions) ko saaf/cancel karne ke liye use hota hai.    

 agr na use kry ye to to memory leakage ho skti hain


